{
  "title": "53: al-Najm النجم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنَّجْمِ اِذَا هَوٰىۙ‏(1)\nWAALNNAJME EZAA HAWAA.\nBy the star when it goeth down\nمَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوٰى‌ۚ‏(2)\nMAA ZALLA SAAHEBOKUM WA MAA GHAWAA.\nErreth not your Companion (Our Apostle Muhammad) nor is he led astray\nوَمَا يَنْطِقُ عَنِ الْهَوٰىؕ‏(3)\nWA MAA YANTEQU A’NIL AL-HAWAA.\nAnd nor he speaketh of (his own) inclination\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا وَحْىٌ يُّوْحٰىۙ‏(4)\nIN HOWA ILLAA WAHAAUN YYOOHAA.\nIt (the wording) is naught but a revelation revealed (unto him)\nعَلَّمَهٗ شَدِيْدُ الْقُوٰىۙ‏(5)\nA’ALLAMAH SHADEEDUL AL-QOOAA.\nTaught him the one Intense in power\nذُوْ مِرَّةٍؕ فَاسْتَوٰىۙ‏(6)\nZOO MERRATIN FAS-TAWAA.\nThe one endued with wisdom; (and) hence he took an overviewing position\nوَهُوَ بِالْاُفُقِ الْاَعْلٰى ؕ‏(7)\nWA HOWA BIL-OFOQIL A-A’LAA.\nWhile he was in the highest horizon\nثُمَّ دَنَا فَتَدَلّٰىۙ‏(8)\nSUMMA DANAA FATADALLAA.\nThen he drew nigh, and became pending\nفَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ اَوْ اَدْنٰى‌ۚ‏(9)\nFA KAANA QAABA QAWSAYNE AW ADNAA.\nThus was (he) the measure between two bows (facing each other) or nigher still\nفَاَوْحٰۤى الٰى عَبْدِهٖ مَاۤ اَوْحٰىؕ‏(10)\nFAAWHAA ALAA A’ABDEH MAA AAWHAA.\nThen revealed He unto His Servant what He did reveal\nمَا كَذَبَ الْفُؤَادُ مَا رَاٰى‏(11)\nMAA KAZABA AL-FUAADU MAA RAAAA.\nBelied not (his) heart what he saw\nاَفَتُمٰرُوْنَهٗ عَلٰى مَا يَرٰى‏(12)\nAAFATUMAAROONAH A’LAA MAA YARAA.\nWhat! Dispute ye then with him as to what he saw?\nوَلَقَدْ رَاٰهُ نَزْلَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(13)\nWA LAQAD RA-AAHO NAZLATAN LAHU.\nAnd indeed he did see him at another descent\nعِنْدَ سِدْرَةِ الْمُنْتَهٰى‏(14)\nI’NDAL SEDRATE AL-MUNTAHAA.\nAt the ‘Sidra’ (the Lotetree) ‘Muntaha’ (the all-Comprehensive Terminus)\nعِنْدَهَا جَنَّةُ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(15)\nE’ENDAHAA JANNATU AL-MAAWAA.\nNigh unto it is the Garden-Abode\nاِذْ يَغْشَى السِّدْرَةَ مَا يَغْشٰىۙ‏(16)\nIZ YAGHSHAN AS-SEDRATA MAA YAGHSHAA.\nWhen covereth (over) the ‘Sidra’ (Tree) that which covereth it\nمَا زَاغَ الْبَصَرُ وَمَا طَغٰى‏(17)\nMAA ZAAGHA BASARO WA MAA TAGHAA.\nNeither his eye did dazzle nor did it rebel\nلَقَدْ رَاٰى مِنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرٰى‏(18)\nLAQAD RAAAA MIN AAYAATIL RABBEHIL KUBRAA.\nIndeed he did see of the greatest signs of his Lord\nاَفَرَءَيْتُمُ اللّٰتَ وَالْعُزّٰىۙ‏(19)\nAFARA-AYTOMUL AL-LAATA WAL U’UZZAA.\nSee ye then (the idols) Lat and the Uzza?\nوَمَنٰوةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الْاُخْرٰى‏(20)\nWAMANAAWTA AS-SAALESATA AL-AUKHRAA.\nAnd Manat, the third (idol) besides?\nاَلَكُمُ الذَّكَرُ وَلَهُ الْاُنْثٰى‏(21)\nAALAKUMU AZ-ZAKARU LAHUL AL-AUNSAA.\nWhat! for you the males and for Him (God) the females?\nتِلْكَ اِذًا قِسْمَةٌ ضِيْزٰى‏(22)\nTILKA EZAL QESMATUN ZEEZAA.\nThis indeed is a division unjust\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَآءٌ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَى الْاَنْفُسُ‌ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰىؕ‏(23)\nIN HEYA ILLAA AASMAAUN SAMMAYTUMOOHAA ANTUM WAABAAUKUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO BEHAA MIN SULTAANIN IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA MAA TAHWAA AL-AANFUSU WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MIN RRABBEHEMU HODAA WA.\nThey are nothing but (mere) names, which have named ye and your fathers, sent not God for them any authority; They follow nothing but a conjecture what their selves are inclined to; and indeed, hath come unto them from their Lord the right guidance\nاَمْ لِلْاِنْسَانِ مَا تَمَنّٰى   ۖ‏(24)\nAM INSAANIK MAA TAMANNAA.\nWhat! Shall man have whatever he wisheth?\nفَلِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةُ وَالْاُوْلٰى‏(25)\nFALILLAAHE AAKHERATO WAL OOLAA.\nNay! God’s is the (life) hereafter and the former (life)\nوَكَمْ مِّنْ مَّلَكٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ لَا تُغْنِىْ شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَنْ يَّاْذَنَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْضٰى‏(26)\nWA MIN MMALAKIN FIL SAMAAWAATE LAA TUGHNEAA SHAFAAA’ATUHUM SHAY-ANW ILLAA MIN BA’DE AN YYAAZANA LAAHO LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YARZAA.\nAnd how many an angel in heavens are whose intercession is of no avail at all save after that permitteth God whomsoever willeth He and chooseth\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ لَيُسَمُّوْنَ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ تَسْمِيَةَ الْاُنْثٰى‏(27)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE LAYUSAMMOONA AL-MALAAAEKATA TASMEETA AL-AUNSAA.\nVerily, those who believe not in the hereafter name the angels with female names\nوَمَا لَهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًاۚ‏(28)\nWA MAA LAHUM BEHI MIN E’ELMIN IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA INNA AZ-ZANNA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL HAQQE SHAY-ANW.\nBut they have not of it anything of knowledge; they follow nothing but a conjecture; verily a conjecture availeth naught the truth at all\nفَاَعْرِضْ عَنْ مَّنْ تَوَلّٰى ۙ عَنْ ذِكْرِنَا وَلَمْ يُرِدْ اِلَّا الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(29)\nFAAA’REZ A’N MAN TAWALLAA A’N ZEKRENAA WA LAM YURED ILLAA HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nTherefore, turn thou aside from him who turneth his back against Our reminder, and desireth not anything but the life of this world\nذٰ لِكَ مَبْلَغُهُمْ مِّنَ الْعِلْمِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ ضَلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ۙ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(30)\nZAA LEKA MABLAGHUHUM MENAL I’LME INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MANIS TADAA.\nThat is the (last) reach of their knowledge; Verily, thy Lord knoweth best of him who is astray from His path and He knoweth best of him who is guided aright\nوَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِۙ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسَآءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰى‌ ۚ‏(31)\nLILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE LE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AASAAOOA BEMAA A’MELOO WAYAJZEAAA LAZEENA AAHSANOOA BIL-HUSNAA.\nAnd God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth, that He may recompense those who do evil for what they did, and that He may recompense those who do good, with what is best\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰٓئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفوَاحِشَ اِلَّا اللَّمَمَ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ‌ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْ اِذْ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاِذْ اَنْتُمْ اَجِنَّةٌ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ‌ۚ فَلَا تُزَكُّوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ‌ ؕ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اتَّقٰى‏(32)\nLAZEENA YAJTANEBOONA KABAAAERA AL-AESME WAL FWAAHESHA ILLAA AL-LAMAMA INNAL RABBAKA WAASEU’U AL-MAGHFERATE HOWA A-A’LAMO BEKUM IZ AN-SHA-A MENAL ARZE WA IZ ANTUM AAJENNATUN FEE BUTOONE MINHUNNA FALAA TUZAKKOOA ANFOSAKUM HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MANIS WAA.\nThose who do avoid the great ones of the sin and shameful deeds save accidentally verily, thy Lord is (the Lord of) vast forgiveness: He knoweth best about you when He raised you from the earth and when ye are embryos in the wombs of your mothers; so assert ye not the purity of your selves; He knoweth best of him who guardeth (himself against evil)\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ الَّذِىْ تَوَلّٰىۙ‏(33)\nAAFARAAYTA LAZEE TAWALLAA.\nHast thou then seen him who hath turned his back\nوَاَعْطٰى قَلِيْلًا وَّاَكْدٰى‏(34)\nWA A-A’TAA QALEELAA WWAAKDAA.\nAnd giveth he a little and withholdeth (his hand)\nاَعِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ الْغَيْبِ فَهُوَ يَرٰى‏(35)\nAAE’ENDAH I’LMUS GHAYBE FAHOWA YARAA.\nWhat! Is with him the know-ledge of the unseen that he seeth\nاَمْ لَمْ يُنَبَّاْ بِمَا فِىْ صُحُفِ مُوْسٰىۙ‏(36)\nAM LAM YUNABBAA BEMAA FEE SOHOFE MOOSAA.\nOr hath he not been told of what is in the scriptures of Moses?\nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ الَّذِىْ وَفّٰىٓ  ۙ‏(37)\nWA IBRAAHEEMA LAZEE WAFFAA.\nAnd of Abraham who fully discharged (his mission)?\nاَلَّا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰىۙ‏(38)\nALLAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU.\nThat no bearer of a burden shall bear the burden of another\nوَاَنْ لَّيْسَ لِلْاِنْسَانِ اِلَّا مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(39)\nWA LLAYSA INSAANIK ILLAA MAA SA-A’A.\nAnd that there is not for man (aught) save what he striveth for\nوَاَنَّ سَعْيَهٗ سَوْفَ يُرٰى‏(40)\nWA ANNAL SAA’YAH SAWFA YURAA.\nAnd that his striving shall soon be seen\nثُمَّ يُجْزٰٮهُ الْجَزَآءَ الْاَوْفٰىۙ‏(41)\nSUMMA YUJZAAHU AL-JAZAAA AL-AAWFAA.\nThen shall he be recompensed to the fullest measure\nوَاَنَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهٰىۙ‏(42)\nWA ANNAL ELAA RABBEKA AL-MUNTAHAA.\nAnd that unto thy Lord is the end (of all)\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَضْحَكَ وَاَبْكٰىۙ‏(43)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AAZHAKA WAABKAA.\nAnd verily He it is Who causeth (one) to laugh and causeth (him) to weep\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَمَاتَ وَ اَحْيَا ۙ‏(44)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AAMAATA WA AAHYAA.\nAnd that He it is Who causeth death and causeth life\nوَاَنَّهٗ خَلَقَ الزَّوْجَيْنِ الذَّكَرَ وَالْاُنْثٰىۙ‏(45)\nWA ANNAHU KHALAQAL AZ-ZAWJAYNE KHALAQAZ WAL AUNSAA.\nAnd He it is Who createth pairs, the male and the female\nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ اِذَا تُمْنٰى‏(46)\nMIN NUTFATIN EZAA TUMNAA.\nFrom the sperm when it is discharged\nوَاَنَّ عَلَيْهِ النَّشْاَةَ الْاُخْرٰىۙ‏(47)\nWA ANNAL A’LAYHE NASH-ATAL AL-AUKHRAA.\nAnd that on Him (alone) is the raising for a second time\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ اَغْنٰى وَ اَقْنٰىۙ‏(48)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA AGHNAA WA AAQNAA.\nAnd that He it is Who enricheth and bestoweth contention\nوَاَنَّهٗ هُوَ رَبُّ الشِّعْرٰىۙ‏(49)\nWA ANNAHU HOWA RABBUL ASH-SHEA’RAA.\nAnd that He it is Who is the Lord of Sirius\nوَاَنَّهٗۤ اَهْلَكَ عَادَا۟ اۨلْٮئُوْلٰى ۙ‏(50)\nWA ANNAHU AHLAKA A’AADAA AL-OOLAA.\nAnd that He did destroy (the powerful) ‘Ad of the ancient (times)\nوَثَمُوْدَا۟ فَمَاۤ اَبْقٰىۙ‏(51)\nWASAMOODAA FAMAA AABQAA.\nAnd Thamood, and He spared not (one to survive)\nوَقَوْمَ نُوْحٍ مِّنْ قَبْلُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا هُمْ اَظْلَمَ وَاَطْغٰىؕ‏(52)\nWA QAWMA NOOHIN MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO HUM AZLAMA WAATGHAA.\nAnd the people of Noah before; Verily they, they were the most unjust and the most transgressing\nوَالْمُؤْتَفِكَةَ اَهْوٰىۙ‏(53)\nWAL MUTAFEKATA AAHWAA.\nAnd the cities overthrown (it is) He (Who) did overthrow\nفَغَشّٰٮهَا مَا غَشّٰى‌ۚ‏(54)\nFAGHASSHAAHAA MAA GHASSHAA.\nSo covered them what did cover\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكَ تَتَمَارٰى‏(55)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKA TATAMAARAA.\nWhich then of the bounties of thy Lord wilt thou dispute about?\nهٰذَا نَذِيْرٌ مِّنَ النُّذُرِ الْاُوْلٰٓى‏(56)\nHAAZAA NAZEERUM MENAL AN-NUZURE AL-AOOLAAA.\nThis (Our Apostle Muhammad) is a Warner of the warners of old\nاَزِفَتِ الْاٰزِفَةُ‌ۚ‏(57)\nAAZEFATE AL-AAAZEFATU.\nDraweth nigh the (Hour of Reckoning which is) ever drawing nigh\nلَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ كَاشِفَةٌ ؕ‏(58)\nLAYSA LAHAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE KAASHEFATUN.\nNone there is for it other than God to lay it bare\nاَفَمِنْ هٰذَا الْحَدِيْثِ تَعْجَبُوْنَۙ‏(59)\nAAFAMEN HAAZAA HAAZAL TAA’JABOONA.\nWhat! Wonder ye then at this statement?\nوَتَضْحَكُوْنَ وَلَا تَبْكُوْنَۙ‏(60)\nWATAZHAKOONA WA LAA TABKOONA.\nAnd laugh ye and not weep?\nوَاَنْتُمْ سٰمِدُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA ANTUM SAAMEDOONA.\nAnd yet sport ye (negligently)\nفَاسْجُدُوْا لِلّٰهِ وَاعْبُدُوْا ۩‏(62)\nFA JODOO LILLAAHE WA BODOO.\nTherefore, prostrate ye in obeisance unto God and worship Him (alone)",
  "merits": "Surah al-Najm (The Star)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 26 verses. The reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of believers and sinners combined. The reciter will lead a respectable and honourable life and people will love and respect him.\nWriting this Surah and keeping it at a talisman makes one courageous in front of the ruler and makes the ruler respect him. He also comes out victorious in debates and discussions."
}
